  steps:
    1. Set grid to 10x10 of zeros.
    2. Pick two distinct non-zero colors for the two frames.
    3. Choose dimensions (h1, w1) and (h2, w2), each in [3, 10], ensuring (h1-2)*(w1-2) != (h2-2)*(w2-2).
    4. Place frame 1 at a random valid position; place frame 2 ensuring no overlap and min gap of 1 empty cell on all sides between the two bounding boxes.
    5. Draw each frame as a 1-cell-thick border of its color on the grid.
    6. Output is a 2x2 grid of the color whose frame has the larger interior area.
  rejection: retry placement if frames cannot fit with required gap (low rejection for 10x10 grid with frames sized 3-10).
